# QA M5 regression (D-075 "Lead-out", D-083, D-086; was
# qa_m5_bug_leadout_camera_snap, fixed in E32; re-cut for D-087): at the
# hand-over from the scroll to the side camera the camera used to snap
# 105 px in one frame (3328 -> 3433), because the side camera re-framed
# Resi at its follow line at once while the right clamp had kept her up to
# 99 px right of it. Since E32 the lead-out camera catches up at most
# `camera.autoscroll_catch_up_speed` = 4 px per frame. The solver route to
# frame 4248: Resi jumps out of the Strobl shallows onto the Strobl quay
# near the right clamp (screen x ~240); the scroll reaches camera x 3328
# (col 208) in step 4242 and from step 4243 the camera moves 4 px a frame
# (3332, 3336, ...) until it has caught up with her. The unit test
# `the_lead_out_camera_catches_up_without_a_snap` (tests/lake.rs) plays
# this replay plus 60 still frames and checks every camera step is 0..=4
# px; the replay format has no camera expectation. The shots show the
# hand-over frame and the next one.
level  = wolfgangsee
seed   = 1
source = handwritten
expect = deaths=0 state=playing
shots  = 4242:handover_before 4243:handover_after
